WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.978
This video shows how to fit the parameters

00:00:02.978 --> 00:00:05.583
of a model to the flow measured at its
outlet,

00:00:05.583 --> 00:00:09.490
and how to check the fitted model on years
that it was not fitted to.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.524
You need a model in Set-up,

00:00:11.524 --> 00:00:15.500
and the flow measured at a point of the
model, one value for each day.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.510
This video uses the basin 01020003.

00:00:21.012 --> 00:00:26.115
In Set-up, click Clear choice and tick the
model 01020003,

00:00:26.115 --> 00:00:29.282
so that it is the only model chosen.

00:00:31.015 --> 00:00:33.725
Click Calibration, the fourth of the four
views.

00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:35.695
The box Model names the model.

00:00:36.195 --> 00:00:38.395
In the bar Method, leave DDS.

00:00:38.896 --> 00:00:42.224
Under Measured data, the page names the
gauge of the model,

00:00:42.224 --> 00:00:44.706
and has the button Download under that
line.

00:00:44.906 --> 00:00:49.456
Until the page has a measured flow, it reads
Choose the measured flow under Checks.

00:00:50.262 --> 00:00:51.292
Click Download.

00:00:51.492 --> 00:00:56.664
Download asks USGS for the days of this
gauge from 1997 to 2025,

00:00:56.664 --> 00:01:01.512
writes them into the folder obs of the
model and reads them.

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:08.142
The page compares the measured flow with the
daily flow of one channel of the model.

00:01:08.342 --> 00:01:10.472
The menu under Where names that channel.

00:01:10.973 --> 00:01:15.093
A calibration divides the years of the
model into three periods.

00:01:15.293 --> 00:01:19.326
The search scores each set of parameter
values on the calibration years,

00:01:19.326 --> 00:01:21.623
and it does not use the validation years.

00:01:22.123 --> 00:01:25.773
This video uses shorter periods so that
the search stays small.

00:01:25.973 --> 00:01:28.873
Under Years, type the years of the three
periods.

00:01:42.232 --> 00:01:45.882
The list Parameters holds the parameters
that the search can change.

00:01:46.082 --> 00:01:50.792
Each parameter has a lowest and a highest
value, and the search stays between them.

00:01:51.293 --> 00:01:53.593
This video leaves the list as it opens.

00:01:54.093 --> 00:01:57.145
The Calibration page calls one run of the
model

00:01:57.145 --> 00:02:00.133
with one set of parameter values a
simulation.

00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:02.093
The search works in iterations.

00:02:02.293 --> 00:02:05.253
The first simulation uses the initial
parameters,

00:02:05.253 --> 00:02:08.153
the values that the model has before the
search.

00:02:08.353 --> 00:02:11.121
Each iteration after it tries a number of
new

00:02:11.121 --> 00:02:14.073
sets of values around the best set found
so far.

00:02:14.573 --> 00:02:18.320
Two boxes under Simulations set the size
of the search:

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.113
Iterations and Simulations per iteration.

00:02:21.313 --> 00:02:26.048
This video sets Iterations to 5 and
Simulations per iteration to 8:

00:02:26.048 --> 00:02:28.593
a small search that shows the steps.

00:02:29.093 --> 00:02:31.823
In Iterations, type 5 and press Enter.

00:02:32.023 --> 00:02:35.623
In Simulations per iteration, type 8 and
press Enter.

00:02:37.725 --> 00:02:39.275
Click Start the calibration.

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:43.568
Under Checks, the page reads Running;
settings locked,

00:02:43.568 --> 00:02:46.887
and the button Stop stands in place of the
start button.

00:02:47.087 --> 00:02:48.497
Watch the block Result.

00:02:48.697 --> 00:02:51.806
Its table has three lines, one for each
step:

00:02:51.806 --> 00:02:55.467
Initial simulation, Iterations and Final
simulations.

00:02:55.968 --> 00:03:00.252
Under the table, the line Best so far
gives the value of KGE daily

00:03:00.252 --> 00:03:03.432
for the best set and the iteration that
found it,

00:03:03.432 --> 00:03:06.288
beside its value for the initial
simulation.

00:03:06.488 --> 00:03:09.589
The tab Progress draws one dot for each
simulation

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.318
and a line through the highest value so
far.

00:03:12.518 --> 00:03:16.908
The box Objective function names the
objective function of the search.

00:03:17.108 --> 00:03:20.122
As the page opens, it holds KGE daily:

00:03:20.122 --> 00:03:24.168
the KGE of the daily flow in the
calibration years.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:29.300
The calibration goes on in the launcher:
this tab may be closed and opened again.

00:03:46.642 --> 00:03:49.762
When the search has ended, the head of
Result reads finished.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:53.023
The box at the top of Result reads
Calibrated.

00:03:53.223 --> 00:03:56.067
The i of the box names the simulation and

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:59.049
the iteration that gave the calibrated
set,

00:03:59.049 --> 00:04:02.793
and the gain in KGE daily over the initial
parameters.

00:04:03.294 --> 00:04:07.164
The table Statistics has a line Initial
and a line Calibrated

00:04:07.164 --> 00:04:10.654
for the calibration years and for the
validation years.

00:04:10.854 --> 00:04:13.409
The search did not use the validation
years,

00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:16.139
so their statistics show how the
calibrated set

00:04:16.139 --> 00:04:18.984
predicts flow in years that it was not
fitted to.

00:04:19.487 --> 00:04:22.870
The chart Daily flow draws three lines:
the measured flow,

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:27.187
the flow with the initial parameters and
the flow with the calibrated set.

00:04:27.688 --> 00:04:30.505
The file calibration.cal in the folder of

00:04:30.505 --> 00:04:33.528
the calibration holds the calibrated
values.

00:04:34.028 --> 00:04:38.798
The next chapter, Uncertainty analysis,
puts a band around the simulated flow.
